# Pairs with HandOffBound. The fence that counts closes is created at the
# initiator's first append rather than at admission. A write admitted before that
# first append reads "no fence yet" as mark 0, a close lands before it is
# dispatched, and mark 0 is stamped at dispatch with the raised generation, above
# the recorded head.
MODULE: HandOffBoundLazyAdmissionMark
TARGET: HandOffBound
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the admission mark's fence is created lazily at the initiator's first append, so an earlier admission carries mark 0 and is stamped at dispatch
PERTURBS: ForeignAdmit, ForeignAlloc, ForeignReject

--- FIND
    /\ fstamp' = fEpoch
    /\ UNCHANGED <<next, author, hoOpen, hoClosedAt, windows, fAdmit, fEpoch, fFence, restarted>>
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: mark 0 until the initiator's first stamped append.
    /\ fstamp' = IF \E o \in Offs : author[o] = "f" THEN fEpoch ELSE 0
    /\ UNCHANGED <<next, author, hoOpen, hoClosedAt, windows, fAdmit, fEpoch, fFence, restarted>>
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ fpend
    /\ fstamp >= fFence
--- REPLACE
    /\ fpend
\* MUTATION: mark 0 is stamped at dispatch.
    /\ (IF fstamp = 0 THEN fEpoch ELSE fstamp) >= fFence
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ fpend
    /\ fstamp < fFence
--- REPLACE
    /\ fpend
    /\ (IF fstamp = 0 THEN fEpoch ELSE fstamp) < fFence
--- END
